                <pb facs="0468" n="412" sameAs="frus:frus1876/pg412"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1 in No. 442.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Arias to Mr. Richardson</hi>.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of Foreign Affairs</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1876-08-31"><hi rendition="#italic">August</hi> 31,
                        1876</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: The President of the republic has
                    considered it proper to appoint Mr. Manuel Romero Rubio, minister of foreign
                    affairs; the general of division, Mariano Escobedo, minister of war and marine;
                    Mr. Juan José Baz, minister of the interior; and Mr. Antonio Tagle, minister of
                    public works, which gentlemen have to-day entered upon the exercise of their
                    duties. In communicating these facts to your honor for your information, I have
                    the honor to reiterate to you the assurances of my distinguished
                    consideration.</p>
                <closer><signed>JUAN DE D. ARIAS.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
